  "notes": "Agricultural Engineering option, University Park (of three options — Food and Biological Processing Engineering, and Natural Resources Engineering are the others, each swapping in different third/fourth-year technical courses, category names, and slot counts -- would need separate degree-plan JSON files to model). Verified 2026-08-27 against the ABE department's real BE Advising Manual (https://abe.psu.edu/undergraduate/resources/advising/be-manual/biological-engineering-course-selection-lists/agricultural-engineering-option), not just the bulletin -- it publishes curated, finite course lists for every elective category (all wired here via 'match' regexes, the same convention as CMPSC's own enumerated technical-elective lists), except 5 BIO/AG-list courses (BRS 350/411/417/423/426) with no BRS catalog in this repo, and ASM 320/420/424 (this repo's asm_catalog.json only has ASM 327) -- both gaps flagged rather than guessed at. CE 465 (department list) appears to be CE 465W in this repo's catalog (probably the same course, W-suffix dropped on the department page) -- used CE 465W. AE 444 and ME 462 are on the department's list but don't exist in this repo's catalogs (likely discontinued/renumbered) -- omitted. Fixed real discrepancy: the bulletin's own Fourth Year table has 0 'Technical Selection' slots in Fall and 2 in Spring -- this plan had them backwards (1 in each) -- corrected, with target_credits updated to the bulletin's real 15.5/15.5 split (previously 18.5/12.5). The Statistics elective ('IE 424, STAT 240/250/318/401/418') is modeled as a single generic slot rather than an enumerated options list (verified against the department manual, complete and accurate), since any of the six satisfies it identically for planning purposes. Post-prereq-parser-fix repair (unrelated to the handbook review, left largely as-is): CHEM 110's real catalog prereq is MATH 22, which was never in this plan, so MATH 21/MATH 22 (Semester 2) were added as an engine-only fallback chain for a hypothetical student with no reported math placement (see expand_math_placement in planner_engine.py). Removed 2026-08-27: MATH 3 and MATH 4 (previously in Semester 1), added on the theory that MATH 21 needs MATH 4 needs MATH 3 -- math_catalog.json's own MATH 21 entry has an empty prereq_groups (no prerequisite at all), and MATH 3/MATH 4 are separately hardcoded as unconditionally satisfied everywhere by expand_math_placement regardless of any student input. They were dead weight inflating the plan by 6 phantom credits with zero effect on schedulability (verified via build_full_plan) -- removed.",
